# Architecture

This repository is a Next.js application starter. App-Framework owns reusable packages, shared Cursor standards, the reusable static deploy workflow, and the capability catalogue. Consume those from their published contract.

- Read `foundation.config.json` for the capabilities this application enables. Leave entries marked `unpublished` or `unavailable` unused.
- Application routes, styling, and configuration values stay in this repository. Public configuration is loaded in `src/config.ts`.
- Import `@app-framework/app-config` and `@app-framework/dev-tools` from the package root only. Leave `@app-framework/ui` disabled until a registry release exists.
- Use published semver ranges. Install them with `pnpm framework:setup` after the registry can resolve them.
- Shared coding rules are the pinned copy in `.cursor/rules/framework/`. Leave that copy unchanged. Product rules belong in the generated application's own `.cursor/rules`.
- Propose a new shared capability in App-Framework when a second application needs the same behaviour.
- Keep optional product features, a component library, and a second catalogue out of this starter.
- `pnpm check` is the full verification. Pre-commit stays limited to lint-staged.
- Deployment is the caller in `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`. It references `Clain-Apps/App-Framework/.github/workflows/deploy-static.yml@main` and skips `Clain-Apps/App-Template`.

The ownership split is documented in `docs/RESPONSIBILITIES.md`.
